From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Rosen Penev <rosenp@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 27 Oct 2026 19:06:48 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: b43: HT-PHY: load the 5 GHz TX gain table at 5 GHz

The TX gain table, entries 0xc0-0x13f of table 0x1a, is the same for
both bands in b43: b43_httab_0x1a_0xc0_late, which is what Broadcom's
driver loads at 2.4 GHz. At 5 GHz Broadcom's driver loads a different
table (traced with mmiotrace on an Apple AirPort Extreme BCM4331 card),
so b43 drives the 5 GHz transmitter with the gains meant for 2.4 GHz.

Add Broadcom's 5 GHz table and load the table of the current band. The
PHY init runs again on every band switch, so the table follows the band.

On that card at 5 GHz, channel 36, HT20, with an MT7612U AP, TCP upload
at MCS 15 goes from 35.6 to 42.5 Mbit/s (still 41% of the frames with a
bad FCS at the AP) and with rate control from 41.7 to 46.6 Mbit/s. The
calibration of the TX I/Q imbalance and LO leakage needs the right
table to work at 5 GHz.

Signed-off-by: Rosen Penev <rosenp@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/net/wireless/broadcom/b43/phy_ht.c    |  4 +-
 .../net/wireless/broadcom/b43/tables_phy_ht.c | 38 +++++++++++++++++++
 .../net/wireless/broadcom/b43/tables_phy_ht.h |  1 +
 3 files changed, 42 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

--- a/drivers/net/wireless/broadcom/b43/phy_ht.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/broadcom/b43/phy_ht.c
@@ -1251,7 +1251,9 @@ static int b43_phy_ht_op_init(struct b43
 		b43_phy_ht_bphy_init(dev);
 
 	b43_httab_write_bulk(dev, B43_HTTAB32(0x1a, 0xc0),
-			B43_HTTAB_1A_C0_LATE_SIZE, b43_httab_0x1a_0xc0_late);
+			B43_HTTAB_1A_C0_LATE_SIZE,
+			b43_current_band(dev->wl) == NL80211_BAND_5GHZ ?
+			b43_httab_0x1a_0xc0_late_5g : b43_httab_0x1a_0xc0_late);
 
 	b43_phy_ht_ext_fem_setup(dev);
 
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/broadcom/b43/tables_phy_ht.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/broadcom/b43/tables_phy_ht.c
@@ -609,6 +609,42 @@ const u32 b43_httab_0x1a_0xc0_late[] = {
 	0x10090001, 0x10090001, 0x10090001, 0x10090001,
 };
 
+/* The same at 5 GHz, as Broadcom's driver loads it on a BCM4331 */
